**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitItemTests`

**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. An item's identity and the model it instantiates, as pure Domain data in the `Kit` module (001 §I '`Kit.Item` = one PHYSICAL piece: `ItemId` (GUID) and an `ItemLabel` (`LP1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `Phone`); the `ItemModel` it instantiates (pinned and snapshotted)'; 001 §A: the kit module holds `Item`, `ItemId`, `ItemLabel`, `Parameter`, `ParameterState`; 001 §I: the model is always an ItemModel version, with an optional typed binding to preset or sample physics; .spec-md §3.14, §3.17, §5 'Kit module'). `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs` (step 122) opens `ItemModels` (step 205), `Library` and `Placement`; the new types are appended at the end of the file in this order, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.1, every case name of two words and no `bool`. (1) `ItemError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the item, the label or the parameter: `InvalidItemLabelErr` (a blank label), `DuplicateItemLabelErr` (another item of the kit has the label's file name), `DuplicateItemIdErr` (another item has the id), `UnknownItemParameterErr` (the item has no parameter of that name) and `InvalidParameterStateErr` (a parameter state breaks its rules, step 214). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the item label is not valid: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that label: <reason>`, `the kit already has an item of that id: <reason>`, `the item has no such parameter: <reason>` and `the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`. (2) `ItemId of Guid` with `.value`, one physical piece's frozen identity, minted by the caller as `KitId` is (step 122). (3) `ItemLabel of string` with `.value`. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<ItemLabel, ItemError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidItemLabelErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), the stem of its `<label>.item-json` (001 §A), so a label keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11). (4) `ItemNotes of string`, free text, empty when there are none. (5) `ItemRevision of int` with `.value`, `static member first : ItemRevision` (1) and `member this.next : ItemRevision`: the revision an item file carries (001 §I 'Revisions'). (6) ItemModelInstance MUST be PresetInstance of model : ItemModelVersionId * preset : ElementValueId | SampleInstance of model : ItemModelVersionId * sample : SampleVersionId | ItemModelVersionInstance of ItemModelVersionId. Every case MUST carry the exact instantiated item-model version. Its entryReferenceOpt MUST always be Some of that model version's entryReference. Its bindingReferenceOpt MUST separately identify the preset or sample physics dependency using the same GUID conversion and snapshot rules as step 137; standalone item models MUST have None. A non-GUID preset binding MUST be rejected by AddItem with InvalidItemModelBindingErr, never erase the model reference. ItemError MUST gain InvalidItemModelBindingErr of reason : string with a diagnostic naming the model and binding.  Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitItemTests.fs`, `module KitItemTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. `an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `ItemLabel.tryCreate "CPL:2"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem "CPL_2"`, equal to `FileStem.ofText "CPL:2"`; `""` and `"  "` answer `InvalidItemLabelErr`. `an item revision starts at one and counts up`: `ItemRevision.first` is 1 and its `next.next` is 3. `an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it`: source, ideal-polarizer and sample instances MUST each return their exact ItemModel version plus a separate physics binding reference; a standalone instance MUST return its model version and no binding.  `every item error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. ItemError MUST also declare UnknownKitItemErr of reason : string, rendered as `the kit has no item of that id: <reason>`, and the error-rendering fact MUST cover it; the S6 copy mapping requires this case.

**Acceptance.** After the item identity lands, `ItemLabel.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank label and name its file through the shared stem rule, and `ItemModelInstance.entryReferenceOpt` MUST answer the reference the kit snapshots; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item label keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `an item revision starts at one and counts up`, `an item's model is referenced as the library snapshots it` and `every item error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fourteen s22 invariants MUST pass. Every item MUST carry an exact ItemModel version, with source/polarizer/sample references treated only as typed physics dependencies; no direct-preset or direct-sample model bypass is permitted.
